// ---------------------------------------------------------------- V8 context

const V8 = `V8 CONTEXT (must map every finding to this):
V8 is a behavior-driven trading intelligence research program for crypto perpetual futures (BTCUSDT 1h). Status: PRE-EXPERIMENTAL / EVIDENCE-BOUND - a falsification program, never a claim of edge. The economic verdict stays NO_ECONOMIC_CLAIM without an authority receipt.
Expert ontology (5 levels): Strategy class -> Mechanism family (causal claim) -> Behavior family (observable pattern) -> Expert hypothesis (expert_id + version) -> Candidate episode.
An Expert is one falsifiable executable hypothesis about one behavior family; it consumes a point-in-time MarketState and emits CandidateDraft; it never submits orders. Parameter/threshold changes are VARIANTS of one family (one multiplicity unit).
EXISTING FORMALIZED experts (src/v8/experts/, one file per family):
- trend_pullback (mechanism trend_continuation, behavior pullback_in_trend, requires trend,volatility,history, LONG): ema_fast>ema_slow and close<ema_slow; entry NEXT_BAR_CLOSE, target_r 1.0, stop_r 1.0, expiry_bars 8, atr_ref; still_valid = uptrend persists.
- failed_breakout (mechanism liquidity_vacuum_reentry, behavior failed_breakout_reentry, requires location,volatility,history, SHORT): close below windowed prior high after a failed breakout; frozen prior_high_ref; still_valid = close stays below ref.
- liquidity_sweep_reclaim (mechanism liquidity_sweep_reclaim, behavior sweep_reclaim, requires location,volatility,history, LONG/SHORT): wick through windowed prior extreme reclaimed by close; frozen ref; still_valid = stays on reclaimed side.
BACKLOG DATA_BLOCKED (no code until derivatives tape): breakout_retest (location,volatility,history), capitulation (trend,volatility,history) - mechanism capitulation_exhaustion.
Feature groups vocabulary: trend, volatility, location, participation, response, liquidity, flow, time, cross_market, history. Feature groups are part of the frozen spec and audited.
Risk: RiskGate deterministic admission; ONE exposure per (instrument, direction); heat cap; risk_geometry = {entry, target_r, stop_r, expiry_bars, atr_ref, frozen refs}; stops and dead-thesis (still_valid) are different exits.
Determinism: no wall clock in replay; event/available/ingested clocks never collapsed; append-only logs; sha1_hex.
Complexity budget (rule 14): max 3 ACTIVE experts + at most one learned component, never both. Router, shared scorer, ranker, learned execution, online learning are ABSENT by default; they enter only through a registry experiment beating the simpler baseline on frozen OOS. Registry status: PROPOSED -> FORMALIZED -> SCREENING -> REPLICATION -> SHADOW -> PROMOTED; REJECTED/MERGED/QUARANTINED/DATA_BLOCKED.
Simulator: canonical Level-1, fill-at-close, STOP_FIRST, gap semantics, Binance USDM cost model.
Evidence labels: LITERATURE_SUPPORTED / PROJECT_EVIDENCE_SUPPORTED / DESIGN_INFERENCE / PROVISIONAL_DECISION / OPEN_QUESTION / REJECTED_OPTION - never interchangeable.
Where findings land in code: src/v8/experts/<family>.py + docs/EXPERTS_REGISTRY.yaml (new family = registry decision + CHANGELOG), src/v8/marketstate.py (feature groups), src/v8/risk.py (RiskGate rules), src/v8/lifecycle.py (episode rules), src/v8/simulator.py (cost model), src/v8/lab.py (runner).`

